# Copy to .env (gitignored) and edit. Every value here has a working default in
# compose.yml; this file exists for the ones that are yours.

# HF_TOKEN=hf_...              # only if you hit a gated repo

# Fraction of unified memory vLLM may claim. 0.84 is the DGX Spark figure from
# MiaAI-Lab. Lower it if a desktop session is running - Xorg and gnome-shell
# hold ~1.2 GB of the SAME pool the model wants (see gx10-status).
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.84

# 1010000 needs YaRN and most of the KV cache budget. Drop to 262144 (native)
# for normal use and you free a lot of memory for concurrency.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144

# THE SPECULATOR, and on this checkpoint it is not a free win.
#
#   mtp    (default)  the checkpoint's own prediction heads. ~55% more decode
#                     tok/s at concurrency 1 - and it disables prefix-cache
#                     reuse ENTIRELY, because this is a hybrid model and vLLM
#                     cannot tell the draft KV group from the mamba ones. A
#                     follow-up turn then re-prefills the whole history.
#   none              prefix caching works. Measured here: a 7.9k follow-up
#                     went 3.53 s -> 0.22 s TTFT, reusing 7840 of 7980 tokens.
#
# Chat and agent use resends the history every turn, so `none` usually wins
# there. One-shot generation is the other way round. Measure yours:
#   BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888/v1 ws up vllm-prefill-ladder --rungs 8000
# SPEC_METHOD=mtp
# SPEC_TOKENS=2
